\f0\fs22 Project Title: AI-Powered Clinical Decision Support System (CDSS) for Chest X-ray Triage\par
Author(s): Vedant and Sakshi\par
Repository: https://github.com/vedant420-s/mini-project\par
Date: April 23, 2026\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 1. Project Overview\b0\f0\fs22\par
This project is an educational web-based clinical decision support system that assists with chest X-ray triage. It combines deep learning and rule-based logic to provide a preliminary NORMAL vs PNEUMONIA prediction, confidence score, symptom assistance, and case management workflow for doctors.\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 2. Objectives\b0\f0\fs22\par
- Build an AI-assisted pipeline for chest X-ray screening.\par
- Provide a doctor-friendly workflow for upload, prediction, and case tracking.\par
- Demonstrate backend, frontend, database, and AI integration in one deployable system.\par
- Maintain clear medical disclaimer and responsible AI boundaries.\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 3. Technology Stack\b0\f0\fs22\par
Backend:\par
- Python, Flask, Flask-SQLAlchemy, Flask-Bcrypt\par
Database:\par
- SQLite\par
AI/ML:\par
- TensorFlow/Keras (MobileNetV2 transfer learning model), Transformers CLIP model\par
Frontend:\par
- HTML, Jinja2 templates, Tailwind CSS classes, JavaScript\par
Utilities:\par
- Pillow/OpenCV for image processing, email providers (Resend/SendGrid/SMTP)\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 4. AI Pipeline\b0\f0\fs22\par
Stage 1: Chest X-ray suitability check\par
- Uses CLIP-based image understanding to reduce non-chest-image misuse.\par
\par
Stage 2: Pneumonia classification\par
- TensorFlow/Keras model predicts NORMAL or PNEUMONIA.\par
- Confidence score and threshold logic are applied in backend routes.\par
\par
Clinical support layer:\par
- Rule-based helper in ai_logic.py creates symptom hints and recommendation summary.\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 5. Core Application Features\b0\f0\fs22\par
- Doctor registration, login, OTP email verification\par
- Upload chest X-ray with optional patient photo\par
- Prediction endpoint with confidence and explanatory message\par
- Case list, case details, and recent/high-risk dashboard sections\par
- AI Helper page for CDSS recommendation support\par
- Patient-facing report lookup flow (project artifact)\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 6. Important Routes\b0\f0\fs22\par
Authentication:\par
- /auth/register\par
- /auth/verify-email\par
- /auth/login\par
- /auth/logout\par
\par
Clinical workflow:\par
- /dashboard\par
- /upload\par
- /predict (POST)\par
- /cases\par
- /cases/<case_id>\par
- /ai-helper\par
- /about\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 7. Model and Performance Notes\b0\f0\fs22\par
Reported academic metrics from project documentation:\par
- Training Accuracy: 92.64%\par
- Validation Accuracy: 87.66%\par
- Test Accuracy: 87.66%\par
\par
Class-wise (reported):\par
- NORMAL: Precision 92.90%, Recall 72.65%, F1 81.53%\par
- PNEUMONIA: Precision 85.49%, Recall 96.67%, F1 90.73%\par
\par
Medical significance:\par
- High pneumonia recall helps reduce missed severe cases.\par
- False positives still require doctor confirmation.\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 8. System Architecture (High Level)\b0\f0\fs22\par
Frontend (Jinja templates + Tailwind UI)\par
-> Flask routes and service logic\par
-> AI model inference + rule-based helper\par
-> SQLite persistence for doctor/patient/case records\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 9. Database Design\b0\f0\fs22\par
Database engine and ORM:\par
- SQLite is used as the default relational database for this academic deployment.\par
- Flask-SQLAlchemy ORM maps Python classes to tables and handles CRUD operations.\par
\par
Schema evolution strategy:\par
- On startup, app.py runs db.create_all() and then executes lightweight ALTER TABLE checks for backward compatibility.\par
- This supports existing local databases when new columns are added in project updates.\par
\par
Entity relationship summary:\par
- Doctor (1 account) -> many authenticated sessions over time (session-managed).\par
- Patient table stores one row per scan case/report, including prediction output and linked media.\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 10. Database Tables\b0\f0\fs22\par
Table: doctors\par
- id (Integer, Primary Key)\par
- name (String 120, required)\par
- email (String 255, unique, indexed, required)\par
- password_hash (String 255, required)\par
- is_verified (Boolean, required, default False)\par
- verification_otp (String 10, nullable)\par
- otp_expires_at (DateTime, nullable)\par
\par
Table: patients\par
- id (Integer, Primary Key)\par
- patient_identifier (String 64, indexed, nullable)\par
- name (String 120, required)\par
- age (Integer, required)\par
- symptoms (Text, required)\par
- generated_symptoms (Text, required, default empty)\par
- image_path (String 500, required)\par
- photo_path (String 500, nullable)\par
- image_blob (LargeBinary, nullable)\par
- image_mime (String 100, nullable)\par
- photo_blob (LargeBinary, nullable)\par
- photo_mime (String 100, nullable)\par
- prediction (String 50, required)\par
- confidence (Float, required)\par
- ai_insights (Text, required, default empty)\par
- created_at (DateTime, required, default UTC timestamp)\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 11. Project Flow Diagram\b0\f0\fs22\par
Doctor workflow (primary):\par
Doctor Register -> Email OTP Verification -> Login -> Dashboard -> Upload X-ray + Patient Details -> Chest X-ray Check (CLIP) -> Pneumonia Prediction (TensorFlow) -> Save Case in Database -> View Case History/Details\par
\par
Patient workflow (report lookup):\par
Enter Patient ID -> Open Patient Reports -> View Report Detail with Prediction + Confidence + AI Insights\par
\par
System processing flow:\par
Input Image -> Preprocessing (resize/normalize) -> Detector Gate -> Classifier Inference -> Rule-based Insight Generation -> JSON/UI Output + Persistent Storage\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 12. Project Files (Core)\b0\f0\fs22\par
- app.py (application setup and startup)\par
- auth.py (authentication and OTP flow)\par
- routes.py (main workflow and API routes)\par
- models.py (database models)\par
- ai_logic.py (CDSS helper logic)\par
- email_utils.py (email notifications)\par
- templates/*.html (UI pages)\par
- models/model.h5, models/xray_detector.h5 (trained artifacts)\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 13. Testing and Validation\b0\f0\fs22\par
- test_app.py validates route and pipeline behavior in an educational setup.\par
- Manual UI tests verify upload, prediction rendering, and case navigation.\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 14. Limitations\b0\f0\fs22\par
- Educational prototype only, not certified for clinical diagnosis.\par
- Binary classification scope (NORMAL/PNEUMONIA only).\par
- Performance depends on image quality and dataset composition.\par
- Requires human clinical oversight in all cases.\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 15. Future Enhancements\b0\f0\fs22\par
- Multi-class disease support and explainability visualizations (e.g., Grad-CAM).\par
- Better calibration and threshold tuning by deployment context.\par
- Docker/cloud deployment with role-based access controls.\par
- Broader datasets and bias/fairness evaluation pipeline.\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 16. Ethical and Responsible AI Statement\b0\f0\fs22\par
This system is designed for academic learning and preliminary assistance only. It does not replace licensed medical professionals. Every output must be verified by qualified clinicians before clinical decisions are made.\par
\par
\f1\fs26\b 17. Conclusion\b0\f0\fs22\par
The project demonstrates a complete end-to-end AI application: model inference, rule-based clinical assistance, secure user flow, and practical web integration. It is a strong academic implementation bridging machine learning and healthcare-oriented software engineering.\par
\par
